comctl32: Group boxes paint without the paint buffer.

Patch 0131 paints themed buttons between BeginBufferedPaint and EndBufferedPaint. The buffer bitmap is created
without being cleared, and GB_ThemedPaint excludes the content rect of a group box, so the interior of a group box
was never written. EndBufferedPaint then copied those undefined pixels over the window, and the group boxes in
Lightroom Classic's Preferences dialog showed black. Group boxes now paint into the paint DC directly, as before
0131. Radio buttons and check boxes keep the buffer.

--- a/dlls/comctl32_v6/button.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32_v6/button.c
@@ -570,7 +570,7 @@
              * DrawThemeParentBackground, gets a memory DC, not the button's paint DC. Lightroom Classic's group
              * boxes call ReleaseDC on the DC they get there, which must not take the paint DC away. */
             GetClientRect(hWnd, &client);
-            if (!wParam && (buffer = BeginBufferedPaint(hdc, &client, BPBF_COMPATIBLEBITMAP, NULL, &paint_dc)))
+            if (!wParam && btn_type != BS_GROUPBOX && (buffer = BeginBufferedPaint(hdc, &client, BPBF_COMPATIBLEBITMAP, NULL, &paint_dc)))
                 hdc = paint_dc;
             btnThemedPaintFunc[btn_type](theme, infoPtr, hdc, drawState, dtflags, infoPtr->state & BST_FOCUS);
             if (buffer)
